package skill

// TraceRootCauseRankOrderTeaching is the short ordering contract shared by
// view discovery, tool schemas, investigation and answer handoff. The full
// effective-impact matrix stays on the tool; this sentence must not become a
// second copy of its row-family pricing rules.
const TraceRootCauseRankOrderTeaching = "Preserve the emitted chain_relevance, channel, and tier. Within each eligible causal lane, compare authorized positive contenders by effective_impact_ms before score. Only rank #1 is primary on the elected causal ladder; an adjacent channel's rank=1 is not a primary cause, and later positive contenders are secondary/tertiary. Raw occupancy does not authorize re-ranking or promotion of context_only/background rows."

// TraceFrameFlowEvidenceTeaching preserves the frame-flow capability without
// mistaking the current sorted-span adjacency producer for a causal connector.
const TraceFrameFlowEvidenceTeaching = "temporal-sequence edges linking one frame's UI/RS/GPU stage spans; latency_ms is a clamped nonnegative gap between temporally ordered spans (overlap may report zero), not measured communication latency. Stage labels do not prove the owning thread's role. Current adjacent-span edges carry causal_conclusion=unproven and are not cross-thread causal proof without an explicit typed connector such as an async cookie, scheduler/IPC edge, or official flow identifier"
